@startuml
title Steam Wrapped - High-Level Component Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor User

package "Client" {
  component "Web Browser" as Browser
  component "Next.js UI" as Frontend {
    component "Profile Search" as Search
    component "Dashboard" as Dashboard
    component "Summary Card" as Summary
    component "Quiz Feature\n(planned)" as Quiz
  }
}

package "Server" {
  component "Express API" as Api
  component "API Routes" as Routes
  component "Steam Service Layer" as Service
  component "In-memory cache\n(currently limited)" as Cache
}

cloud "Steam Web API" as Steam
database "Persistent database\n(out of scope)" as Database

User --> Browser
Browser --> Frontend : HTTPS / page requests
Frontend --> Routes : /api/search\n/api/profile/:steamid
Routes --> Service : validate and delegate
Service --> Steam : fetch profile and game data
Service --> Cache : short-lived response reuse
Cache ..> Service : optional cache hit
Service --> Routes : JSON profile/stats
Routes --> Frontend : JSON response

Search --> Dashboard : navigate to profile
Dashboard --> Summary : generate stats card
Dashboard --> Quiz : launch quiz\n(planned)
Quiz ..> Service : future quiz data

Database ..> Service : future persistence\n(not implemented)

note right of Cache
Caching is deliberately small and
in-memory. It reduces duplicate
Steam calls without adding an
operational data store.
end note

note right of Database
No database is required for the
current product scope. The app
retrieves public Steam data on
demand and does not aggregate
large historical datasets.
end note

@enduml
